ta-v-849fe8c0="" src="https://cdn-images.toolify.ai/n8n/icon/ghostTool.svg" alt="Ghost Tool" class="el-image__inner" style="object-fit: cover;" width="16" height="16"><!----></div></div> <span data-v-578d8737="" class="text-gray-1000 group-hover:text-purple-1300">Ghost Tool</span></a><a data-v-578d8737="" href="https://www.toolify.ai/n8n/node/Sticky_Note-891" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-2 py-1 group"><div data-v-578d8737="" class="w-7 h-7 bg-gray-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span data-v-578d8737="" class="w-4 h-4 flex items-center justify-center node-icon-svg"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 640 640"><!--! Font Awesome Free 7.1.0 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license/free (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License) Copyright 2025 Fonticons, Inc. --><path fill="currentColor" d="M160 544C124.7 544 96 515.3 96 480L96 160C96 124.7 124.7 96 160 96L480 96C515.3 96 544 124.7 544 160L544 373.5C544 390.5 537.3 406.8 525.3 418.8L418.7 525.3C406.7 537.3 390.4 544 373.4 544L160 544zM485.5 368L392 368C378.7 368 368 378.7 368 392L368 485.5L485.5 368z"></path></svg></span></div> <span data-v-578d8737="" class="text-gray-1000 group-hover:text-purple-1300">Sticky Note</span></a><a data-v-578d8737="" href="https://www.toolify.ai/n8n/node/Brave_Search_Tool-1030" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-2 py-1 group"><div data-v-578d8737="" class="w-7 h-7 bg-gray-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><div data-v-849fe8c0="" data-v-578d8737="" class="el-image w-4 h-4 object-cover flex items-center justify-center avatar-image"><img data-v-849fe8c0="" src="https://cdn-images.toolify.ai/n8n/icon/braveSearchTool.svg" alt="Brave Search Tool" class="el-image__inner" style="object-fit: cover;"><!----></div></div> <span data-v-578d8737="" class="text-gray-1000 group-hover:text-purple-1300">Brave Search Tool</span></a></div></div> <section data-v-578d8737="" class="mt-12 space-y-8"><div data-v-578d8737=""><h2 data-v-578d8737="" class="text-2xl font-semibold">
              Who is this best for?
            </h2> <div data-v-578d8737="" class="mt-3 leading-8 text-424242 markdown-content"><ul><br><li>Content agencies looking to scale high-quality article production.</li><br><li>Blog managers needing an end-to-end automation solution for Ghost CMS.</li><br><li>Technical SEO specialists who require optimized content and structured data.</li><br><li>n8n users seeking advanced examples of LangChain Agent orchestration.</li><br></ul></div></div> <div data-v-578d8737=""><h2 data-v-578d8737="" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Overview</h2> <div data-v-578d8737="" class="mt-3 leading-8 text-424242 markdown-content"><p>Generating high-quality, SEO-optimized blog content requires multiple stages: research, drafting, optimization, editing, and publishing. This often involves manual handoffs and significant time investment. This powerful n8n workflow solves this by implementing an 'Agentic' system where a central <code>Blog Content Orchestrator Agent</code> manages the entire process. By delegating complex tasks—such as external research via Brave Search, detailed SEO analysis, and final HTML preparation—to dedicated AI specialists, this solution ensures consistency, speed, and technical compliance. It leverages various language models (GPT-4, Claude) for best-in-class output and uses specialized n8n node configurations for reliable, production-ready content delivery directly into your Ghost CMS.</p></div></div> <div data-v-578d8737=""><h2 data-v-578d8737="" class="text-2xl font-semibold">How it Works</h2> <div data-v-578d8737="" class="mt-3 leading-8 text-424242 markdown-content"><p>This highly complex n8n workflow is structured around seven distinct phases, all managed by the central orchestrator agent.</p><p></p><ol><br><li><strong>Trigger and Orchestration:</strong> The process starts with the <code>When chat message received</code> n8n trigger. A user provides a topic, and the <code>Blog Content Orchestrator Agent</code> takes control, determining the required parameters (style, length, chapter count).</li><br><li><strong>Research &amp; Planning:</strong> The orchestrator delegates to the <code>Research Agent</code>, which utilizes Brave Search, Brave News, and the internal Ghost Content n8n node to perform competitive and topical analysis. It then generates a structured Table of Contents (TOC) and research insights.</li><br><li><strong>Content Generation:</strong> Once the TOC is approved, the <code>Blog Content Generation Agent</code> writes the full article draft. It enhances the research provided by conducting sectional searches via Brave Search, ensuring the content is current and cited.</li><br><li><strong>SEO Optimization:</strong> The raw draft is passed to the <code>SEO Optimizer Agent</code>. This agent performs dedicated keyword research, generates optimized meta titles, descriptions, and schema markup, ensuring high visibility for the final post. It uses the Brave Search n8n node extensively, adhering to critical 2-second delays between search queries.</li><br><li><strong>Editorial Review:</strong> The optimized content moves to the <code>Blog Content Editor Agent</code>, which focuses purely on readability, flow, citation verification, and clean HTML structure, turning the SEO draft into a final, polished version.</li><br><li><strong>Publication Preparation:</strong> The <code>Blog HTML Publisher Agent</code> generates the complete HTML document, including all necessary metadata, Open Graph tags, and technical SEO elements.</li><br><li><strong>Final Action:</strong> The final output is automatically published as a 'draft' post to the configured Ghost CMS using the dedicated Ghost publisher tool n8n node, ready for final human review and scheduling. This entire automated journey transforms a single request into a publication-ready asset, demonstrating the power of agentic n8n templates.</li><br></ol><p></p></div></div> <div data-v-578d8737=""><h2 data-v-578d8737="" class="text-2xl font-semibold">
              Installation Guide
            </h2> <div data-v-578d8737="" class="mt-3 leading-8 text-424242 markdown-content"><p>To deploy this comprehensive n8n workflow, follow these steps:</p><p></p><ol><br><li><strong>Import the n8n workflow:</strong> Copy the provided JSON data and paste it into your n8n instance using the 'New' &gt; 'Import from JSON' option.</li><br><li><strong>Set up Credentials:</strong> This n8n workflow requires several credentials due to the heavy reliance on external tools and multiple AI models:</li><br></ol>    <em>   <strong>OpenAI API Key:</strong> Used by the GPT-4 and GPT-4o models across the agents.<br>    </em>   <strong>Anthropic API Key:</strong> Used by the Claude models, often as fallback or alternative language models.<br>    <em>   <strong>Brave Search API Key:</strong> Essential for the <code>Brave Search tool</code> n8n node used by the Research, Generation, and SEO Agents for real-time information gathering.<br>    </em>   <strong>Ghost CMS Admin API Key:</strong> Required for the <code>Ghost publisher tool</code> n8n node to create and update posts directly in your Ghost instance.<br>    *   <strong>Ghost CMS Content API Key:</strong> Used by the Content n8n node for internal content analysis (checking for existing posts).<ol><br><li><strong>Activate the Trigger:</strong> Ensure the <code>When chat message received</code> n8n trigger is active. Once credentials are set up, you can start testing by interacting with the designated chat interface.</li><br></ol><p></p></div></div> <div data-v-578d8737=""><h2 data-v-578d8737="" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Node Details</h2> <div data-v-578d8737="" class="mt-3 leading-8 text-424242 markdown-content"><p>This n8n workflow utilizes advanced LangChain and dedicated integration nodes:</p><p><em>   <strong>When chat message received (n8n trigger):</strong><br>    </em>   <strong>Function:</strong> Serves as the interactive trigger for the workflow, typically receiving a topic request from a user via a chat interface.<br>    <em>   <strong>Key Configuration:</strong> Configured for <code>streaming</code> responses to handle long-running operations.<br></em>   <strong>Blog Content Orchestrator Agent:</strong><br>    <em>   <strong>Function:</strong> The core management unit. It orchestrates the flow through multiple phases, ensuring data integrity and delegation to the specialized agents.<br>    </em>   <strong>Key Configuration:</strong> System message defines the entire 7-phase content process, including data validation requirements and strict handling of the Brave Search 2-second delay constraint.<br><em>   <strong>Research Agent:</strong><br>    </em>   <strong>Function:</strong> Conducts initial topic research, competitive analysis, and generates the detailed Table of Contents (TOC) based on live data.<br>    <em>   <strong>Key Configuration:</strong> Directly connected to <code>Brave Search2</code>, <code>Brave News</code>, <code>Blog Content tool</code>, and both OpenAI and Anthropic language models (GPT-4o, Claude Haiku) for robust research capability.<br></em>   <strong>SEO Optimizer Agent:</strong><br>    <em>   <strong>Function:</strong> Performs deep SEO analysis on the draft, generating optimized meta tags, H1s, and JSON-LD schema markup.<br>    </em>   <strong>Key Configuration:</strong> Utilizes the <code>Brave Search</code> n8n node for keyword research and competition analysis, ensuring compliance with the specified delay rules.<br><em>   <strong>Blog Content Editor Agent:</strong><br>    </em>   <strong>Function:</strong> Refines the SEO-optimized draft, enhancing readability, verifying all citations, and producing clean, structured HTML.<br>    <em>   <strong>Key Configuration:</strong> Can use <code>Brave Search4</code> for additional source verification if required, maintaining citation quality.<br></em>   <strong>Blog HTML Publisher Agent:</strong><br>    <em>   <strong>Function:</strong> Finalizes the publication process by calculating reading time, generating the final HTML wrapper, and executing the Ghost publication.<br>    </em>   <strong>Key Configuration:</strong> It is critically connected to the <code>Ghost publisher tool</code> n8n node for post creation, setting the initial status to 'draft'.<br><em>   <strong>Ghost publisher tool (n8n node):</strong><br>    </em>   <strong>Function:</strong> The final action, utilizing the Ghost Admin API to create the blog post, injecting the optimized title, slug, content, and meta description generated by the Publisher Agent.<br><em>   <strong>OpenAI Chat Model nodes &amp; Anthropic Chat Model nodes:</strong><br>    </em>   <strong>Function:</strong> Provide the underlying LLM intelligence for reasoning, analysis, and writing across all specialized agents. The n8n workflow leverages high-performance models like GPT-4o and Claude 3.7 Sonnet.</p></div></div></section> <div data-v-578d8737="" class="flex items-center mt-12 gap-8"><a data-v-578d8737="" href="https://www.toolify.ai/n8n/sitemap-crawler-to-vector-db-for-rag-knowledge-base" class="md:h-[56px] flex-1 flex items-center p-4 bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors"><div data-v-578d8737="" class="w-6 h-6 flex items-center justify-center"><svg data-v-31f12e78="" data-v-578d8737="" aria-hidden="true" class="w-6 h-6 flex-shrink-0 svg-icon" style="stroke: unset;"><use data-v-31f12e78="" xlink:href="#icon-caret-left"></use></svg></div> <span data-v-578d8737="" class="text-gray-800 text-sm ml-2">Sitemap Crawler to Vector DB for RAG Knowledge Base</span></a> <a data-v-578d8737="" href="https://www.toolify.ai/n8n/comprehensive-instagram-api-tool-server-for-ai-agents" class="md:h-[56px] flex-1 flex items-center p-4 bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors justify-end text-right"><span data-v-578d8737="" class="text-gray-800 text-sm mr-2">Comprehensive Instagram API Tool Server for AI Agents</span> <div data-v-578d8737="" class="w-6 h-6 flex item